---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { installCommand } from "../data/install";
---
<Layout title="Quickstart — Torana" description="Install Torana and route a coding agent through your local proxy.">
  <article class="frame prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Quickstart · local machine</p>
    <h1 class="display">Traffic through Torana in five minutes.</h1>
    <p>Torana is pre-1.0. Use it on a development machine first, keep the listener on loopback, and review each plugin’s requested capabilities before enabling it.</p>
    <h2>1. Install</h2>
    <pre><code>{installCommand}</code></pre>
    <p>Torana is intentionally unversioned today. For a reproducible deployment, replace <code>main</code> with a reviewed commit SHA.</p>
    <h2>2. Create local configuration</h2>
    <pre><code>./torana --debug</code></pre>
    <p>On first run Torana imports <code>config.json</code> into managed state in your user configuration directory. Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080/_torana/</code> to edit providers. The listener and control plane default to loopback. Leave the server running, then verify it from another terminal:</p>
    <pre><code>curl --fail-with-body --silent http://127.0.0.1:8080/health</code></pre>
    <p>A healthy process returns <code>{`{"status":"ok"}`}</code>. A failed plugin reload keeps the last known-good pipeline serving but reports a degraded health status.</p>
    <h2>3. Send one inference request</h2>
    <pre><code>{`curl --fail-with-body --silent \\
  http://127.0.0.1:8080/provider/deepseek/v1/chat/completions \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $DEEPSEEK_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Reply with: torana is ready"}]}'`}</code></pre>
    <p>This uses the built-in DeepSeek route and forwards your caller credential only to that selected provider. Configure a different provider in the control plane if you do not use DeepSeek.</p>
    <h2>4. Point your harness at it</h2>
    <pre><code>export OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/provider/deepseek/v1</code></pre>
    <p>Replace <code>deepseek</code> with the provider name in your configuration. The harness must speak that provider’s supported wire format; see the <a href="/docs/support/">exact endpoint and harness matrix</a>. Auxiliary provider endpoints pass through without entering the plugin pipeline.</p>
    <h2>5. Explore plugins</h2>
    <pre><code>./torana plugin install --official</code></pre>
    <p>Torana clones the official source, builds each selected plugin locally, and prints its digest. Installation does not approve or enable anything: inspect the exact manifest and capability set in the control plane, approve that digest, then add the plugin to the ordered pipeline.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
